====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[step]] or [[climb]] onto or otherwise [[enter]] a [[ship]], [[aircraft]], [[train]] or other [[conveyance]].
#: {{ux|en|It is time to '''board''' the aircraft.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1862|author=Benjamin J. Totten|title=Naval Text-Book, and Dictionary, for the use of the Midshipmen of the U.S. Navy
|passage=You '''board''' an enemy to capture her, and a stranger to receive news or make a communication.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 November 2|author=Paul Bigland|title=New trains, old trains, and splendid scenery|journal=RAIL|issue=969|page=57|text=I have just enough time for a "swifty" in the reopened (but on this day just about to close) '301' bar on Platform 4 before '''boarding''' a two-car Northern Class 158 working the 1824 to Leeds.}}
#: {{antonyms|en|alight|disembark}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[provide]] someone with meals and lodging, usually in [[exchange]] for [[money]].
#: {{co|en|to '''board''' one’s horse at a livery stable}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[receive]] meals and lodging in exchange for money.
#* '''February 8, 1712''', Charity Frost, ''The Spectator'' No. 296 (letter to the editor)
#*: We are several of us, gentlemen and ladies, who '''board''' in the same house,
# {{senseid|en|capture}} {{lb|en|transitive|nautical}} To (at least attempt to) [[capture]] an [[enemy]] ship by going [[alongside]] and [[grappling]] her, then [[invading]] her with a [[boarding party]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[obtain]] meals, or meals and [[lodging]]s, [[statedly]] for compensation
# {{lb|en|transitive|now|rare}} To [[approach]] (someone); to make advances to, [[accost]].
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|II|iv|text=Ere long with like againe he '''boorded''' mee, / Saying, he now had boulted all the floure {{...}}}}
# To [[cover]] with boards or [[boarding]].
#: {{co|en|to '''board''' a house}}
#* {{RQ:Cowper Task|text=the '''boarded''' hovel}}
# To [[hit]] (someone) with a [[wooden]] board.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To write something on a board, especially a [[blackboard]] or [[whiteboard]].

